  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI9. Share of zero-emission buses and mini-buses as part of public transportation fleet</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-03-29" value="5.9%" year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-03-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="8%">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is on track and target has been achieved.  There is an upcoming survey to be finalised by September 2025. Per public statistics, there are currently 5,542 vehicles of public transport, out of which 514 are electrical vehicles (per information from Managing Authorities), which is about 9% of the total.

This indicator measures the increase of the total stock of vehicles of categories M1, M2, and M3 owned by rural and urban counties and/or used for public passenger transport, that are zero-emission vehicles.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="9%"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">People with enhanced resilience to climate risks</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-06-15" value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-06-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="3,700000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is on track. 

This indicator measures the cumulative number of people benefitting from enhanced disaster and climate response. The response network will be expanded by establishing new fire/paramedic and intervention units (from current 284 to 299), logistics centers (from current three to seven), and increasing the number of professional emergency response staff in GIES and CIES (by 800).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI6. Number of people that benefit from investments to reduce flood risk</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-06-15" value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-06-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="480,000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is on track. 

This indicator measures the cumulative number of people living in Areas of Potential Significant Flood Risk who benefit from high priority prevention and protection measures to reduce flood risk, as prioritized in Romania&apos;s second cycle Flood Risk Management Plans and as reported to the European Commission in September 2023.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI4. Number of people that benefit from improved access to early warning (cumulative)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-06-15" value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-06-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="450,000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is on track. 

This indicator measures the number of people benefitting from the expansion of the early warning system through the establishment of 500 new sirens for hydrometeorological hazards and other emergencies, implemented by the &#x2018;&#x2019;Romanian Waters&#x2019; Agency under the MEWF.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI2. Number of people with disabilities with completed self-preparedness plans for emergencies (cumulative)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-06-15" value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-06-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="10,000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is on track. 

This indicator measures the total number of people registered with disabilities who have benefited from pilot multi-hazard preparedness trainings and awareness activities and have developed a Personal Plan for emergencies.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI7. Share of prioritized high seismic risk class I schools that have been improved for safety, resilience, and energy efficiency</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-06-15" value="0%" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-06-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="30%">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is in progress. 

This indicator measures the share of 46 prioritized high seismic risk (class I) schools that are rehabilitated/reconstructed under the &#x201c;Safe and Healthy Schools&#x201d; Government program.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0%"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI3.Share of intervention units nationwide with first responders equipped with knowledge on how to identify GBV cases and employ effective referral mechanisms to link survivors with essential services</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-06-15" value="0%" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-06-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="90%">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is on track. 

This indicator measures the share of intervention units nation-wide with first responders who receive GBV training in relevant format/delivery mode, as well as the number of trained intervention units.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0%"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI5. The updated general procedures for the national RO-ALERT warning system have been approved by the National Committee for Emergency Situations (NCES)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-06-15" value="No" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-06-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-14"></period-end>
     <target value="Yes">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation is on track. 

This indicator will capture the following modernization reforms for RO-ALERT EWS: (i) linking RO-ALERT with other EWS to improve the speed of warning, especially for meteorological hazards; (ii) updating sound alerts considering the potential impact on the population; and (iii) modernizing communication to make it more accessible to vulnerable groups, including people with disabilities, and to offer improved information on resources to prevent and/or address cases of GBV in disasters/crisis.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="No"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
